{
    "background_story": "Dr. Journi was a brilliant microbiologist who spent her career studying antibiotic resistance. Her breakthrough research on polymyxin, a last-resort antibiotic, led to a deeper understanding of its mechanisms and limitations. Journi's work focused on developing new strategies to revive the effectiveness of polymyxin against increasingly resistant bacterial strains. Her tireless efforts in the lab and collaborations with international experts resulted in the development of a novel polymyxin-based treatment. This innovation has since saved countless lives, particularly in hospitals where antibiotic-resistant infections had become a growing concern. Journi's dedication to combating antibiotic resistance has earned her numerous accolades, including the prestigious Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine. Her work continues to inspire a new generation of scientists to tackle the pressing issue of antimicrobial resistance.",
